{
  "area": "turks-caicos-grand-turk",
  "method": "Grand Turk (the Columbus Landfall wall and its shore reefs), Salt Cay and South Caicos. Grand Turk: Blue Water Divers' published dive site map (33 sites, read from its Google My Maps layer) against the Visit Turks and Caicos tourism board's 2026 dive sites map (14 sites); Grand Turk Diving publishes no site list, Oasis Divers' domain is an under-construction page and the shop is reported closed, and the Turks & Caicos Reef Fund mooring list covers only the Caicos Bank, so no official list was found. Salt Cay: the tourism board map against Salt Cay Divers' 'a few of our dive sites' line, which is a partial list. South Caicos: the tourism board map against East Bay Resort's dive page (Wayback capture of 2023; the 2019 capture adds the Subway), which names only three sites; the Salterra resort's dive centre publishes none. Each operator or board counts once; a site is counted when named, divable and on at least two, with spelling variants merged (Rookery is the board's The Rockery; Northwest Drop-Off is North West Wall; Shark Point Canyon is Shark Point, which is an assumption; Wanderlust is Wandalust). Excluded: sites on one list only, and the generic 'South Caicos Wall'. Positions are omitted because the operator map's pin coordinates disagree with its own descriptions. The South Caicos and Salt Cay denominators are thin because no second operator list could be read. Counted 2026-10-14.",
